index 137118a..dd93b0b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -260,6 +260,49 @@ There are a few important things to be aware of when using WebSockets for stream
     ```
   - The decoder will be detected and used automatically.
 
+## Japanese keyboards
+
+The web client supports Japanese (JIS) keyboards. It sends the physical key
+positions to the host, so the **host has to use a Japanese keyboard layout**
+(e.g. `setxkbmap jp` or the equivalent setting of your desktop environment).
+
+The JIS specific keys (`ろ`, `¥`, `かな`, `変換`, `無変換`) are marked as
+"non normalized" and Sunshine needs the following upstream changes to translate
+them (none of them is released yet):
+
+- [LizardByte/Sunshine#5542](https://github.com/LizardByte/Sunshine/pull/5542)
+- [LizardByte/libvirtualhid#101](https://github.com/LizardByte/libvirtualhid/pull/101)
+
+Build Sunshine with both changes:
+
+```sh
+git clone --recursive https://github.com/LizardByte/Sunshine
+cd Sunshine
+
+# Sunshine side
+git fetch origin pull/5542/head:pr-5542
+git checkout pr-5542
+
+# libvirtualhid side (git submodule)
+cd third-party/libvirtualhid
+git fetch origin pull/101/head:pr-101
+git checkout pr-101
+cd ../..
+
+cmake -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
+cmake --build build
+```
+
+If the build fails because the libvirtualhid version is too old, merge the PR
+branch on top of the current libvirtualhid master instead
+(`git checkout master && git merge pr-101`) or lower
+`LIBVIRTUALHID_MINIMUM_VERSION` in Sunshine's `CMakeLists.txt`.
+
+On released Sunshine versions (without those changes) the `ろ` key types `<>`
+and the `¥` key types `]`.
+
+The `半角/全角` key works without the Sunshine changes.
+
 ## Config
 The config file is under `server/config.json` relative to the executable.
 Here are the most important settings for configuring Moonlight Web.
